        'Keep **reads** in a data-access layer used by Server Components, **writes** in Server Actions, and UI split into server-first components with small client islands.\n\n- `app/(shop)/` - public route group with the shop layout (header, footer)\n- `app/(shop)/products/[slug]/` - page.js, loading.js, opengraph-image.js\n- `app/admin/` - protected layout + pages; `actions.js` for Server Actions\n- `app/api/` - only `auth/[...nextauth]` and a public `products` JSON API for external clients\n- `lib/` - `prisma.js`, `data/products.js` (cached reads), `validation/product.js` (zod), `env.js`\n- `components/` - `ProductCard`, `Pagination`, `SearchBox` (client), `SubmitButton` (client)\n- `auth.js`, `middleware.js`, `prisma/schema.prisma`, `e2e/`\n\nAnalogy: a restaurant. Server Components are the kitchen (data, heavy work), Client Components are the waiters (interaction), Server Actions are order slips going back to the kitchen, the data layer is the pantry, middleware is the host at the door.',
